  <prompt>Clear every typecheck error in src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/** and src/client/office-addins/shared/services/**, so FR-18's clean-typecheck criterion becomes reachable and Phase 1's adapter work starts from a clean compile. These are the host-abstraction and auth/API seams, so the type-level-only rule is strict here: task 010 (FR-04 adapter consolidation) will restructure WordAdapter afterwards and must not inherit a half-restructure from this task.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. TypeScript strict-mode remediation across an Office.js host-adapter abstraction and an NAA-based auth/API client layer. You are correcting types, not restructuring the adapter seam. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>`npm run typecheck` in src/client/office-addins reports zero errors for every file under shared/adapters/** and shared/services/**; `npm run build` and `npm test` are green; the error counts in the directories this task does NOT own are unchanged from the task 001 baseline; the adapter seam is structurally unchanged so task 010 inherits exactly the code plan.md finding F-e describes; and the fix patterns used are appended to projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-18 (spec.md line 92) requires clearing the pre-existing typecheck debt in src/client/office-addins first, so new errors are visible during feature work. Four strict options in src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json drive the debt: `noUnusedLocals` (line 16), `noUnusedParameters` (line 17), `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` (line 20) and `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` (line 21). This task owns two small but structurally important directories. shared/adapters contains IHostAdapter.ts, HostAdapterFactory.ts, WordAdapter.ts, OutlookAdapter.ts, types.ts, index.ts and a __tests__ folder with OutlookAdapter.test.ts and WordAdapter.test.ts. shared/services contains AuthService.ts, ApiClient.ts, authenticatedJsonFetch.ts, index.ts and a __tests__ folder with ApiClient.test.ts. Two facts constrain the work sharply. First, plan.md finding F-e: `HostAdapterFactory.registerAdapter()` has zero call sites, the registry is empty, `create()` always throws INVALID_HOST, both taskpanes construct their adapter directly, and shared/adapters/WordAdapter.ts still uses the known-broken `body.getOoxml()` path that word/WordHostAdapter.ts documents as the 2026-09-03 UAT defect. Task 010 fixes all of that in a prescribed order. This task must leave that situation exactly as it found it, only compiling. Second, ADR-028 is arch-test enforced on shared/services/AuthService.ts: auth is NAA via `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`, and MSAL construction must never appear in this package.</background>
