  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/** and src/client/office-addins/shared/services/** ONLY, plus src/client/office-addins/shared/__mocks__/** IF AND ONLY IF task 001's rollup reports the UNASSIGNED bucket as confined to that path (it is adapter and service test scaffolding, so it belongs with this task). If the UNASSIGNED bucket contains anything else, do NOT absorb it — escalate. Do NOT edit any file under shared/taskpane/**, word/** or outlook/**; tasks 006 and 008 own those and run concurrently. A cross-boundary edit is both a merge conflict and a lost fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the adapter seam. This task MUST NOT pre-empt task 010 (FR-04). Specifically: do NOT port `getCompressedFile()` from word/WordHostAdapter.ts into WordAdapter.ts; do NOT add any `registerAdapter()` call site or otherwise activate `HostAdapterFactory`; do NOT change which adapter a taskpane constructs; do NOT delete or deprecate any adapter; and do NOT "fix" the known-broken `body.getOoxml()` path in WordAdapter.ts. Task 010 does all of that in a prescribed order for a documented reason (plan.md finding F-e). Your diff must leave the structure identical and only the types corrected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: every fix in this task. Fix types PROPERLY. MUST NOT use `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, or a blanket non-null assertion (`!`) applied merely to silence a diagnostic. MUST NOT relax src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json — `strict`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noUnusedLocals` and `noUnusedParameters` all stay exactly as they are. tsconfig.json is OUT OF SCOPE for this task and for 006 and 008.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: every fix in this task. This is a TYPE-LEVEL change only. MUST NOT change runtime behaviour: no altered conditional, no changed default value, no changed Office.js call sequence, no altered error-mapping, no removed retry or timeout. The adapters wrap Office.js and the services wrap fetch and token acquisition — both are places where a "harmless" tidy-up changes what the host or the BFF actually receives. If an error can only be resolved by a behaviour change, STOP and escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">SCOPE: shared/services/AuthService.ts and anything it touches. Auth is NAA via `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`; MSAL construction lives inside that strategy, never in this package. MUST NOT introduce `new PublicClientApplication`, `createNestablePublicClientApplication`, or `.WithClientSecret` while resolving a type — these are arch-test enforced and a violation fails CI regardless of whether it compiles. If a type error tempts you toward constructing an MSAL object to satisfy a signature, that is an escalation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: dependencies. MUST NOT add, remove or upgrade any npm dependency to satisfy a type, and MUST NOT modify package.json or package-lock.json. Note in particular that `@azure/msal-browser` is a direct dependency of this package (package.json line 22) — do NOT begin importing from it to fix a type; that is the ADR-028 violation wearing a different hat.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE: shared/adapters/__tests__/ and shared/services/__tests__/. These are inside the tsconfig include globs, so their errors count toward this task. Fix their types the same way as production code. MUST NOT delete, skip or `xit` a test to make typecheck pass (KEEP-path violation under docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md). WordAdapter.test.ts and OutlookAdapter.test.ts are the only automated coverage the host seam has before task 010 restructures it — weakening them removes the safety net that task 010 depends on.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE: import resolution while fixing types. This project holds a recorded Path A exception: the add-in consumes `@spaarke/auth` only. MUST NOT resolve a missing type by importing from `@spaarke/ui-components` (NFR-03 — some of it is Xrm-bound and breaks at runtime in an Office host).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: build verification. `npm run build` IS the production build in this package — there is no `build:prod` script (package.json line 7). src/client/office-addins/CLAUDE.md line 39 names `build:prod` in error.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>TypeScript strict-mode remediation; Office.js host adapters; NAA auth and fetch clients</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-baseline.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md</file>
