  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a completed `npm install`, when `npm run typecheck` is run in src/client/office-addins and the output is filtered to paths under shared/adapters/ and shared/services/, then zero errors are reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given task 001 reported the UNASSIGNED bucket as confined to shared/__mocks__/**, when the same typecheck output is filtered to shared/__mocks__/, then zero errors are reported. Given task 001 reported UNASSIGNED as empty, this criterion is vacuously satisfied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same typecheck run, when the per-directory counts for shared/taskpane/, word/ and outlook/ are compared against the task 001 baseline, then none has increased.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm test` exits 0 with suite and test counts greater than or equal to the task 001 baseline, and WordAdapter.test.ts, OutlookAdapter.test.ts and ApiClient.test.ts all still execute.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff` on shared/adapters/ shows no `registerAdapter()` call site added, no `getCompressedFile()` ported in, no adapter deleted, no change to which adapter a taskpane constructs, and no change to the `body.getOoxml()` path — the seam is structurally identical to its pre-task state (plan.md finding F-e; task 010 owns all of it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `grep` across the diff finds no newly added `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `grep` across the diff finds no `new PublicClientApplication`, no `createNestablePublicClientApplication`, no `.WithClientSecret`, and no new import from `@azure/msal-browser` (ADR-028, arch-test enforced).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff` shows src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json, package.json and package-lock.json unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff --name-only` lists no file under shared/taskpane/, word/ or outlook/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no import from `@spaarke/ui-components` was added (ADR-012 Path A exception, NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All four ui-tests below pass and their results are recorded, including the dark-mode check in both directions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md contains a section headed for task 007 that records the fix shapes used and confirms the adapter seam was left structurally unchanged for task 010.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Step 9.5 code-review and adr-check gates ran and their findings are resolved or explicitly accepted.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec reference: FR-18 (line 92), FR-04 (line 64), NFR-03 (line 100), Success Criterion 12 (line 209). Plan reference: section 4 Phase 0 tasks 006-008, finding F-e, Phase 1 task 010, risk R-4.

No `&lt;justification&gt;` block is present: this is a modify-only task. It adds no new service, abstraction, endpoint, DI registration, package or column — CLAUDE.md section 11's gate does not apply to edits of existing files.

Parallel-safety within the P0-typecheck wave: 006 owns shared/taskpane/**, 007 owns shared/adapters/** plus shared/services/** (plus shared/__mocks__/** conditionally), 008 owns word/** plus outlook/**. The three directory sets are disjoint. The shared surfaces are node_modules (read-only concurrency, fine) and projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md — task 006 creates it and 007/008 append their own clearly headed sections, so keep edits additive and scoped to your own heading. tsconfig.json is out of scope for all three, which removes the one file they would otherwise contend for.

Sizing note: shared/adapters contained 8 .ts files and shared/services 5 at authoring time — the smallest shared bucket by file count, but the highest-consequence one per file. The task 001 rollup, not this note, is the authority on the error count.

Downstream: task 010 (FR-04 adapter consolidation, prescriptive mode) and task 013 (FR-01 client — adds `canGetDocumentUrl` and `getDocumentUrl()` to IHostAdapter) both build directly on this directory. Leaving it compiling but structurally untouched is the deliverable.</notes>

